===Point out the fake Fu Xuan{{subst:void|<!--202050202-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Memory-Alchemy Commission|update|As the Matrix of Prescience Ultima starts its calculations, March 7th returns to the not-too-distant past.<br />For her own safety, she should first complete the homework Fu Xuan assigned.<br />Thankfully, the task isn't too hard. She just has to figure out who is the real master diviner out of the two before her.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Fu Xuan With Hand on Hip)
:'''March 7th:''' Miss Fu Xuan? Is that you?
:'''Memory-Fu Xuan:''' If we want to resolve the Stellaron crisis, we must refine the question: What is the crux of the problem? Generally, it is believed that when one seizes on the crux of a problem, the problem will split open like bamboo on the edge of a knife.
:'''Memory-Fu Xuan:''' Nobody could have foreseen the catalyzing effect of the Stellaron on the Ambrosial Arbor. As the ancients said, blessings bring about misfortune, and vice versa. Nature has its own algorithm, and it is precisely when fate wends betwixt blessing and misfortune that I, a master diviner of masterful proportions, am called on to save the people of the Luofu!
:'''March 7th:''' What the heck is she talking about? Master Diviner, did you actually say that at the time? I can't remember.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' It would appear that in Miss March's estimation, I'm somewhat of a... blabbermouth.
:'''March 7th:''' N&mdash;No! Uh &mdash; I've always seen you as a... m&mdash;masterful master diviner! Hehe...
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Despite the obvious distortions in this experience, the base materials from which it is composed are taken from your actual memory &mdash; there is no falsehood here. In other words, your subconscious mind thinks that I... talk in tongue-twisters.
:'''March 7th:''' Hahaha... Uh, &mdash; it's mainly just that I, uh... can't always comprehend the... lofty ideals and, uh... principles you discuss...
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Forget it, now is not the time for losing one's temper.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' If the inferred experience is distorted, we should focus on filtering out each distortion one by one &mdash; otherwise we won't be able to trace your memories back any further.
:'''March 7th:''' Umm, this is getting a little complicated... Is there a... simpler explanation?
:'''Fu Xuan:''' *sigh* Draw your bow and fire an arrow at that Fu Xuan.
;(Enter battle)
::{{tx|Enemy list missing}}

;(Talk to Welt Yang)
:'''March 7th:''' Mr. Yang! Hi there!
:'''Memory-Welt:''' March, get ready. The next fight is going to be very dangerous.
:'''March 7th:''' Huh? Which next fight?
:'''Memory-Welt:''' Stay focused. Phantylia is headed for the Ambrosial Arbor &mdash; if we don't stop the Lord Ravager, it'll be a catastrophe.
:'''March 7th:''' Okay, alright. Got it.
:'''Memory-Welt:''' Another thing... The future is what's most important for us. Don't you agree, March?
:'''March 7th:''' What?
:'''Memory-Welt:''' Dwelling on memories can numb your sense of the present, and inhibit future ambitions.
:'''March 7th:''' Miss Fu Xuan, do people in memories always say weird stuff like this?
:'''Fu Xuan:''' The distortions we're experiencing are... unorthodox.
